From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: support native linux riscv64 hosts

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to project-chip/connectedhomeip]

Two places in the GN build only know about the Linux CPUs upstream
already builds on (x64, x86, arm, arm64), so a native riscv64 host
can't generate the build at all:

- build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn picks the default Linux toolchain as
  //build/toolchain/linux:linux_${target_cpu}_${compiler}, which on a
  riscv64 host is linux_riscv64_gcc, but build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn
  never defines it. Every target then fails to resolve with "needs
  //build/toolchain/linux:linux_riscv64_gcc()", starting with the
  `gn gen` Pigweed's bootstrap runs to install the Python packages.
  Add it next to the existing ones. It mirrors linux_x64_gcc rather
  than the cross-prefixed arm/arm64 ones, since this is a native build
  with the host gcc/g++/ar; build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn has no
  riscv64-specific flags to add (its "riscv" branch is the embedded
  FreeRTOS one), so the compiler's own rv64gc/lp64d defaults apply.
- chip_enable_python_modules defaults to false unless host_cpu is x64,
  arm64 or arm, which leaves //src/controller/python:chip-repl out of
  the graph (and rejects chip_python_package_prefix as an unused arg
  under gn_gen.sh's --fail-on-unused-args). Add riscv64 to that list,
  the same way arm was added for Raspbian.

src/controller/python/BUILD.gn already falls back to cpu_tag =
current_cpu, so the wheel comes out as *_riscv64 with no change there.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 BUILD.gn                       | 3 ++-
 build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index 465eccc..88be251 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@ if (current_toolchain != "${dir_pw_toolchain}/default:default") {
   declare_args() {
     chip_enable_python_modules =
         (current_os == "mac" || current_os == "linux") &&
-        (host_cpu == "x64" || host_cpu == "arm64" || host_cpu == "arm")
+        (host_cpu == "x64" || host_cpu == "arm64" || host_cpu == "arm" ||
+         host_cpu == "riscv64")

     # Build the Linux all clusters app example with default group
     chip_build_all_clusters_app = false
diff --git a/build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn b/build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn
index abc61ab..5f912cf 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn
@@ -91,3 +91,11 @@ gcc_toolchain("linux_arm64_clang") {
     is_clang = true
   }
 }
+
+gcc_toolchain("linux_riscv64_gcc") {
+  toolchain_args = {
+    current_os = "linux"
+    current_cpu = "riscv64"
+    is_clang = false
+  }
+}
--
2.50.1
